  "scope": "Sound minigame note dealing, pair resolution, row scrolling, pop motion and drawing readability.",
  "changes": [
    "Replace misleading speed with pitchCount in DealNotes and name pattern, note/pair counts, duplicate detection, layout coordinates and pair-use pointers.",
    "Name row sizes, columns, previous slots and last surviving notes in the scrolling/reveal logic. Name queued-note touch state and the explicit bank/group decomposition.",
    "Name note/pop cursors, reset slots, motion velocities/direction, rise and scale values, and drawing matrix sine/cosine components. Verify the Hud_RenderSprite last argument as priority against its definition.",
    "Apply consistent formatting to scene methods and remove redundant this qualifiers while retaining explicit this->* member-pointer dispatch. Correct Behavior state descriptions and explain the packed pair queue."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "dealing": "data_ov006_0212ee10 bounds random pitch selection; data_ov006_0212ee18 gives note count and half is pair count. Pair usage is capped at two during placement. Pattern3 selects a group of three consecutive pitches with a random cyclic start.",
    "rows": "RevealUnmatched scans two table-sized rows and remembers the last alive slot in each. Note_StateScroll derives a column by repeated row-size subtraction, then starts preceding alive notes when their horizontal gap is at most four pixels.",
    "pair_queue": "Note_StateOpening packs slot << 8 and pitch + 1 into each queue entry. CheckPair compares the low bytes after its timer and uses the upper bytes to update the corresponding slots.",
    "motion_and_drawing": "Pop handlers read native velX/velY, scale and direction fields; renamed locals keep their existing arithmetic and reloads. DrawPops builds its matrix from trig table entries0/1 and scale. Hud_RenderSprite in d_s_mg_base.cpp names and forwards its fifth parameter as priority to OAM rendering.",
    "ownership": "Queue21 state466f7b7436b71e6ce75368547cb96829fa7a615e had no active Sound class/file reservations or overlaps across ov006 text0x02119904..0x0211cbd0, init0x02132970..0x02132f68, ctor0x021335d4..0x021335d8 and bss0x02142cc0..0x02142e88. These are the complete production delinks ranges.",
    "runtime_validation": "No new emulator run was necessary for local names supported by explicit arithmetic and API forwarding. No new artwork identity, original class name or unknown-field semantics are asserted.",
    "retained_constraints": [
      "Keep the note/pop cursor views and split-base address arithmetic; prior DrawNotes native-state and DealNotes native-pair-array +8-byte failures remain documented.",
      "Keep all casts, volatile table-pointer reads, pragmas, function order, PMF tables, explicit slot argument to SpawnPops and the existing lifecycle implementation.",
      "Keep unknown pop byte+0x1f unknown; no header, symbol, manifest, data or production ownership changes."
    ]
